The test report must include:
1. Test Identification — test name, date, component, test facility
2. Test Objective — what was being verified
3. Test Configuration — setup, instrumentation, environmental conditions
4. Test Procedure — step-by-step procedure followed
5. Results — measured values, pass/fail criteria, observed behavior
6. Data Summary — key metrics in tabular form
7. Anomalies — any deviations from expected behavior (state "None observed" if clean)
8. Conclusion — overall assessment and recommendation for acceptance
9. NPR Compliance — note how the test satisfies applicable NPR verification requirements

